       Question
 Locate all files (excluding directories) owned by user john within the /home/usersdata directory on App Server 2. Copy these files while preserving the directory structure to the /beta directory.
      Solution
1- Login into app server 2
    ssh steve@stapp02
2-Locate all files owned by john (excluding directories)
 Use find with -type f to restrict results to files only:
    sudo find /home/usersdata -type f -user john
.-type f → ensures only files are matched
-.user john → restricts ownership to user john
3-Copy files to /beta while preserving directory structure
 Pipe the results into cp --parents:
    sudo find /home/usersdata -type f -user john -exec cp --parents {} /beta \;
.cp --parents → recreates the directory hierarchy relative to /home/usersdata
.Destination /beta will contain the same structure as source
4-Validate the copy
  Check that files exist under /beta:
    sudo find /beta -type f -user john
  compare counts
    sudo find /home/usersdata -type f -user john | wc -l
    sudo find /beta -type f -user john | wc -l

   
